          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "keshâvarz is a native Persian word, inherited rather than borrowed; it is usually traced to Middle Persian kišāwarz, \"farmer\". It is usually explained as built on keš-, \"to plough\"."
            }
